<BaseLayout title="about" narrow>
  <h1>about this garden</h1>

  <p>
    This is Mark's working notebook. Notes, embedded experiments, half-formed
    thoughts. Some written directly, some drafted by an agent (look for the
    badge). Roughness is the feature — most pages are intentionally short and
    intentionally unfinished.
  </p>

  <p>
    The structure borrows from <a href="https://notes.andymatuschak.org">Andy
    Matuschak's notes</a>: atomic notes, aggressive linking, visible growth
    states. There's no publish-vs-draft distinction beyond a flag in
    frontmatter.
  </p>

  <h2>growth states</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>seedling</strong> — just captured, rough, possibly wrong.</li>
    <li><strong>budding</strong> — edited at least once, idea is shaping up.</li>
    <li><strong>evergreen</strong> — durable, well-linked, I'd point someone at it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>provenance</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>by hand</strong> — written directly.</li>
    <li><strong>by agent</strong> — drafted by an agent, possibly lightly edited.</li>
    <li><strong>human + agent</strong> — substantive back-and-forth.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    The agent is a Claude instance reading <code>AGENTS.md</code> at the repo
    root for voice and tag taxonomy. Most agent notes are short. Some get
    promoted to budding or evergreen later.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
